From fec8a6227e76b575e0095a19639a655fe61a279a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: J P <jpwatters@mac.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 16:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 38/41] web: Radio source window with Find NAS, like the Tab5's
 drawer

The web page's "Radio source" entry only offered a prompt for typing the
NAS address; the Tab5's drawer section also has Find NAS. Now the Radio
menu entry opens a small window with the current source and its state,
Find NAS (lists every relay that answers, each with a Use button), a
typed address with Use NAS, and Use USB.

The search is the Tab5's own radio_relay_discover() (QMXR? on UDP 7355).
It blocks for ~1.5 s and the web server answers every request from one
task, so POST /api/relay/find starts it on a short-lived task and the page
polls GET /api/relay/find:
  {"searching":false,"result":2,"found":[{"ip":"10.0.0.137","port":7355},...]}
(result -1: WiFi down; 0: no relay answered.)

Tested in a browser against a mock Tab5 (find, pick, typed address with
port, back to USB); webserver.c compile-checked; check_web and check_webui
clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
